WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.542 --> 00:00:19.926
I tied up the canoe in its usual place and decided to sleep in it, but I couldn't

2
00:00:19.966 --> 00:00:20.487
sleep much.

3
00:00:21.947 --> 00:00:25.049
Every time I woke up, I thought somebody had me by the neck.

4
00:00:26.189 --> 00:00:28.670
Finally I decided that I couldn't live this way.

5
00:00:29.931 --> 00:00:33.312
I had to search until I found out who was on Jackson's Island with me.

6
00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:39.043
I paddled my canoe along the shore of the island, keeping close to land.

7
00:00:40.324 --> 00:00:45.147
The moon shone almost as bright as day, but I didn't see anything moving on the shore.

8
00:00:46.488 --> 00:00:49.590
When I got to the other end of the island, I landed the canoe.

9
00:00:51.991 --> 00:00:53.592
By now it was almost morning.

10
00:00:54.433 --> 00:00:58.976
With my gun in my hand, I moved quietly through the woods to the place where I had

11
00:00:59.036 --> 00:01:00.377
seen the campfire ashes.

12
00:01:01.378 --> 00:01:04.700
After a little while, I saw the light of a campfire through the trees.

13
00:01:06.012 --> 00:01:10.415
As I crept closer, I saw a man lying on the ground with a blanket over him.

14
00:01:11.456 --> 00:01:13.658
It was Miss Watson's black slave Jim!

15
00:01:15.279 --> 00:01:16.800
I called out, "Hi, Jim!"

16
00:01:17.481 --> 00:01:18.761
and skipped out of the trees.

17
00:01:19.942 --> 00:01:23.425
He jumped up and stared at me wildly as if I were a ghost.

18
00:01:24.666 --> 00:01:27.208
Then he moaned, "Don't hurt me!

19
00:01:27.868 --> 00:01:29.509
I've never harmed a ghost.

20
00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:32.832
You get right back in that river again!"

21
00:01:34.652 --> 00:01:39.336
I quickly made Jim understand that I wasn't dead and that I was very glad to see him.

22
00:01:40.677 --> 00:01:43.680
I told him that I trusted him not to tell anyone where I was.

23
00:01:47.563 --> 00:01:51.967
Jim told me that he'd been on the island since the night after I was killed, with nothing

24
00:01:51.987 --> 00:01:52.948
to eat but berries.

25
00:01:54.229 --> 00:01:55.450
Now he was very hungry.

26
00:01:57.071 --> 00:01:58.593
We walked together to my canoe.

27
00:01:59.874 --> 00:02:04.653
I got out my cornmeal, bacon and coffee, a frying pan, and a coffeepot.

28
00:02:05.994 --> 00:02:10.657
While Jim got a fire going and cooked bacon and cornmeal, I caught a catfish.

29
00:02:11.978 --> 00:02:15.120
Jim cleaned and fried it, and we had a delicious breakfast.

30
00:02:16.241 --> 00:02:18.102
Then we lay in the grass, relaxing.

31
00:02:20.684 --> 00:02:24.707
After a while, Jim asked who had been killed in that cabin, if it wasn't me.

32
00:02:26.168 --> 00:02:28.749
I told him the whole story of how I tricked everyone.

33
00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:32.412
Then I asked him why he was camping on the island.

34
00:02:33.408 --> 00:02:36.611
Jim looked very uneasy and didn't say anything for a minute.

35
00:02:37.712 --> 00:02:41.795
Then he said, "You won't tell anyone about me, will you?"

36
00:02:43.397 --> 00:02:44.418
I promised I wouldn't.

37
00:02:45.799 --> 00:02:48.801
"Well, Huck—I ran away."

38
00:02:49.822 --> 00:02:50.503
I was shocked.

39
00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:53.305
Black slaves belonged to their owners.

40
00:02:54.446 --> 00:02:56.848
It was against the law for slaves to run away.

41
00:02:57.689 --> 00:03:00.772
But I would never break my promise to Jim, and I told him so.

42
00:03:02.108 --> 00:03:04.990
Then Jim explained why he had run away from Miss Watson.

43
00:03:06.631 --> 00:03:13.174
"Miss Watson promised that she wouldn't sell me, but I saw a slave trader at her house recently,

44
00:03:13.614 --> 00:03:15.135
and I began to get uneasy.

45
00:03:16.336 --> 00:03:22.859
One night I went past the house, and I heard Miss Watson tell the Widow Douglas that she

46
00:03:22.919 --> 00:03:25.581
was going to sell me for eight hundred dollars.

47
00:03:27.021 --> 00:03:31.504
I didn't wait to hear any more—I just ran away down to the river.

48
00:03:33.644 --> 00:03:35.285
I hid in a shack until morning.

49
00:03:36.345 --> 00:03:41.226
I thought maybe I could steal a rowboat, but there were people around all the time.

50
00:03:42.367 --> 00:03:46.128
I heard your Pap and other people talking about how you'd been murdered.

51
00:03:47.168 --> 00:03:49.228
I was very sorry to hear it, Huck.

52
00:03:50.689 --> 00:03:53.150
I was hungry, but I wasn't afraid.

53
00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:59.831
I knew Miss Watson and the widow were going to be out all day, so they wouldn't notice

54
00:03:59.851 --> 00:04:01.472
that I was gone until evening.

55
00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:07.902
When it got dark, I walked along the river until I came to a place with no houses.

56
00:04:09.622 --> 00:04:14.084
I realized that if I stole a boat, people would know I'd taken it.

57
00:04:15.044 --> 00:04:19.025
What I wanted was a raft of those logs that float down the river.

58
00:04:20.145 --> 00:04:25.567
When I saw one, I swam out to it, climbed on, and lay down on the wood.

59
00:04:26.767 --> 00:04:32.363
The river was moving fast, and I expected to be forty kilometers away by morning.

60
00:04:33.563 --> 00:04:35.585
But I didn't have good luck.

61
00:04:36.566 --> 00:04:40.568
Men with lanterns in their boats came after me, looking for me.

62
00:04:41.869 --> 00:04:47.013
When one of them got so close that he would see me, I slid off the raft and

63
00:04:47.093 --> 00:04:48.274
swam to this island.

64
00:04:49.275 --> 00:04:52.517
I decided to stay here until the men stopped looking for me.

65
00:04:53.658 --> 00:04:58.669
I had some matches in my hat where they wouldn't get wet, so I could make a fire.

66
00:04:59.670 --> 00:05:00.591
I was all right."

67
00:05:02.973 --> 00:05:08.258
Just then some young birds came along, flying short little distances and landing often.

68
00:05:09.359 --> 00:05:11.821
Jim said it was a sign that it was going to rain.

69
00:05:12.962 --> 00:05:14.223
Jim knew lots of signs.

70
00:05:15.144 --> 00:05:19.848
For instance, he said you shouldn't count the things you are going to cook for dinner, because that

71
00:05:19.888 --> 00:05:20.769
will bring bad luck.

72
00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:24.312
And you shouldn't shake a tablecloth after sundown.

73
00:05:26.092 --> 00:05:30.976
"Jim, it seems as if all the signs you know are about bad luck," I said.

74
00:05:30.996 --> 00:05:33.778
"Don't you know any good luck signs?"

75
00:05:35.259 --> 00:05:37.061
"Very few," he replied.

76
00:05:37.081 --> 00:05:40.223
"Why do you need to know if good luck is coming?

77
00:05:40.864 --> 00:05:42.145
Do you need to keep it away?"

78
00:05:44.527 --> 00:05:49.691
Then he told me that if a man had hairy arms and a hairy chest, it meant he

79
00:05:49.731 --> 00:05:51.132
was going to be rich someday.

80
00:05:52.488 --> 00:05:56.314
Jim had hair on his arms and chest, so I asked him if he was rich.
